<title>ITALY: Italian oil products use down 1.4 pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>Italian oil products use down 1.4 pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian consumption of refined oil products fell 1.4 percent to 94.8 million tonnes in 1996, compared with 1995 figures, according to preliminary data from trade group Unione Petrolifera.</p>
<p>  Category			1996 (000 tonnes)  Chg vs 1995</p>
<p>  Total				  94.8		-1.4 pct</p>
<p>  Fuel oil			     27.2		+1.1 pct</p>
<p>  Vehicle petrol		     17.7		+1.1 pct</p>
<p>  Total car diesel		   15.9		-4.2 pct</p>
<p>  Petrolchemical useage	     7.5		-3.8 pct</p>
<p>  Total heating oil		   3.8		+5.6 pct</p>
<p>  Other				  22.7		-1.7 pct</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
